(LAW 5 – The Referee) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Authority) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each match is controlled by a referee who has full authority to enforce the Laws of the) Tj
T*
(Game in connection with the match.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The referee's decision on facts connected with play, including whether a goal is scored) Tj
T*
(and the result of the match, is final. The referee may not change a restart decision) Tj
T*
(when play has restarted or the referee has signalled the end of the first or second) Tj
T*
(half.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Duties) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The referee enforces the Laws of the Game, controls the match in cooperation with other) Tj
T*
(match officials, and acts as timekeeper, keeping a record of the match.) Tj
T*
() Tj
