(LAW 11 – Offside) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Offside Position) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A player is in an offside position if any part of the head, body or feet is nearer to) Tj
T*
(the opponents' goal line than both the ball and the second-last opponent. The hands and) Tj
T*
(arms of all players, including the goalkeepers, are not considered.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A player is not in an offside position if the player is level with the second-last) Tj
T*
(opponent or the last two opponents, or is level with or behind the ball.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Offside Offence) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A player in an offside position at the moment the ball is played or touched by a) Tj
T*
(team-mate is only penalised on becoming involved in active play by interfering with) Tj
T*
(play, interfering with an opponent, or gaining an advantage by playing the ball or) Tj
T*
(interfering with an opponent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There is no offside offence if a player receives the ball directly from a goal kick, a) Tj
T*
(throw-in, or a corner kick.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Page 4 of 7) Tj
T*
ET
