(LAW 12 – Fouls and Misconduct) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Direct Free Kick) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A direct free kick is awarded if a player commits any of the following offences against) Tj
T*
(an opponent in a manner considered by the referee to be careless, reckless or using) Tj
T*
(excessive force: charges, jumps at, kicks or attempts to kick, pushes, strikes or) Tj
T*
(attempts to strike, tackles or challenges, or trips or attempts to trip.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Handball) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A player is penalised for handball only if they deliberately touch the ball with their) Tj
T*
(hand or arm. Making the body unnaturally bigger is not, by itself, an offence unless the) Tj
T*
(arm is also clearly away from the torso when the ball strikes it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It is not usually an offence if the ball touches a player's hand or arm directly from) Tj
T*
(their own head or body, including when the arm is close to the torso.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Denial of a Goal or an Obvious Goal-Scoring Opportunity) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Where a player denies the opposing team a goal or an obvious goal-scoring opportunity by) Tj
T*
(a handball offence, the player is sent off wherever the offence occurs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Where a player commits an offence against an opponent within their own penalty area) Tj
T*
(which denies an obvious goal-scoring opportunity and the referee awards a penalty kick,) Tj
T*
(the offender is cautioned if the offence was an attempt to play the ball. In all other) Tj
T*
(circumstances, including holding, pulling, pushing, or not attempting to play the ball,) Tj
T*
(the offending player is sent off.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
